# Dev-Platform Architecture

## Overview

The platform provides deterministic, reproducible development environments
for multiple tenants via a layered architecture:

```plantuml
@startuml dev-platform-architecture
!theme cerulean

package "Client Layer" {
  [Browser]
  [IDE Plugin]
}

package "Gateway" {
  [Port Authority :9000] as PA
  [TLS Proxy (Caddy)] as PROXY
}

package "Control Plane (Python FastAPI)" {
  [Manager Agent :8001] as MGR
  [Editor Agent :8002]  as EDIT
  [Verifier Agent :8003] as VER
  [RAG Service :8004]   as RAG
  [Presence WS :8005]   as PRES
  [DTG Classifier :8006] as DTG
}

package "Data Plane (Zig / Nim / Rust)" {
  [Snapshot Engine :9090] as SNAP
  [CAS Store] as CAS
  [NBD Exporter :10809] as NBD
  [CRDT Library (libcrdt.so)] as CRDT
}

package "Security" {
  [gVisor] as GVISOR
  [seccomp BPF] as SECCOMP
  [eBPF Auditor] as EBPF
  [OverlayFS] as OVERLAY
}

package "Observability" {
  [OTel Collector] as OTEL
  [Kafka :9092]    as KAFKA
  [ClickHouse]     as CH
}

package "Storage" {
  database "Nix Store\n(OverlayFS)" as NIXSTORE
  database "GCS Bucket\n(CAS + Embeddings)" as GCS
  database "Pinecone Index" as PINECONE
}

Browser --> PROXY : HTTPS
IDE Plugin --> PROXY : HTTPS
PROXY --> PA : allocate port
PA --> MGR : route
PA --> EDIT : route
PA --> VER  : route

MGR --> RAG  : context retrieval
MGR --> DTG  : guidance classification
MGR --> EDIT : POST /apply /build
MGR --> VER  : POST /test

EDIT --> SNAP : JSON-RPC fork/write/commit
EDIT --> CAS  : chunk storage
VER  --> SNAP : JSON-RPC read
VER  --> NBD  : block device mount

SNAP --> CAS
CAS  --> GCS  : remote chunk storage
RAG  --> PINECONE : vector search
RAG  --> CAS  : content retrieval

PRES --> CRDT : merge ops

SNAP -.-> GVISOR
GVISOR -.-> SECCOMP
EBPF -.-> GVISOR

MGR  --> OTEL : traces
EDIT --> OTEL : traces
VER  --> OTEL : traces
OTEL --> KAFKA
KAFKA --> CH

NIXSTORE --> OVERLAY
@enduml
```

## Data Flow: Plan → Build → Verify

1. **User request** arrives at Manager (`POST /plan`).
2. Manager queries **RAG** for source-code context (≤ 32 k tokens).
3. Manager sends augmented prompt to **OpenAI** → task list.
4. For each task the **DTG Classifier** analyses stdout/stderr and injects
   a micro-instruction (e.g. `[[GUIDANCE: RETRY_BUILD]]`) into the next LLM call.
5. `edit_code` tasks are delegated to **Editor**:
   - Snapshot Engine **forks** the base snapshot (copy-on-write).
   - Diff is applied, chunks stored in **CAS**.
   - Snapshot is **committed** atomically via `renameat2`.
6. `run_build` tasks call `nix build` inside the forked snapshot,
   loading environment from the ≤ 50 ms Nix env cache.
7. `verify_ui` tasks run **Playwright** headless browser inside the snapshot,
   and **Potemkin Detector** scans the DOM.
8. All spans flow to **OpenTelemetry Collector** → Kafka → ClickHouse.

## Security Model

| Layer | Mechanism | Default policy |
|---|---|---|
| Syscall filter | seccomp BPF | `SCMP_ACT_KILL` (allowlist only) |
| Container kernel | gVisor ptrace/KVM | network=false, mount=false |
| Filesystem | OverlayFS | nosuid, nodev, noexec |
| Audit | eBPF kprobe on execve | Log to perf ring buffer |
| Networking | Port Authority + iptables DNAT | Ephemeral port 20000–
